# india.kb — India: its states, rivers, monuments, institutions, people and festivals.
#
# `geography.kb` has India as one line among forty countries; `history.kb` has the Maurya and
# Mughal empires, Gandhi and Independence. Neither has a state, a river beyond the Ganges, a
# constitutional office, or a single one of the things a general-knowledge question about India
# actually asks for.
#
# It belongs in this corpus for a plain reason: `njp/tongue.py`, `njp/dialects.py` and
# `tests/njp/test_hinglish.py` say this brain is expected to work in Hindi and Hinglish, and a
# system that reads "Ganga kahan hai" and holds nothing about the Ganga answers in the right
# language and says nothing.
#
# `capital` and `located_in` are functional here as everywhere, so each state carries exactly one
# capital and each place exactly one location.

# --- the country ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
Republic of India | is_a=country | is_a=federal republic | located_in=South Asia | capital=New Delhi | currency=Indian rupee | has_property=the most populous country in the world | has_property=a parliamentary democracy
